1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,720
These are the unluckiest lucky people.

2
00:00:01,879 --> 00:00:05,519
So a man named Bill Morgan was unluckily in a horrific car accident that almost took his life,

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:07,200
but after surviving a 12-day coma,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,259
he celebrated by purchasing a scratch-off ticket and he actually won a car.

5
00:00:10,419 --> 00:00:12,679
Afterwards, when it was actually being covered by a local news station,

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,800
he reenacted it and won another $250,000 from a scratch-off.

7
00:00:15,939 --> 00:00:18,719
A man purchased a gold egg at a flea market for $13,000,

8
00:00:19,079 --> 00:00:21,250
hoping to flip it quickly for a $1,000 profit,

9
00:00:21,519 --> 00:00:23,980
but he unfortunately couldn't and went into serious debt over this.

10
00:00:24,120 --> 00:00:28,359
Luckily though, later on he stumbled on the fact that it was the lost third imperial Easter egg made for

11
00:00:28,359 --> 00:00:32,340
the Russian Tsar, so he ultimately sold it for $33 million a couple months later.

12
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,939
A woman named Joan Murray fell from 14,000 feet after her parachute failed,

13
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:37,259
and by all accounts she should have died,

14
00:00:37,399 --> 00:00:39,640
but she actually landed on a mound of fire ants which stung her,

15
00:00:39,719 --> 00:00:43,399
giving her intense pain that sent adrenaline to her heart, keeping her alive long enough to get help,

16
00:00:43,399 --> 00:00:44,420
and she ultimately survived.

17
00:00:44,619 --> 00:00:48,299
And finally, in 1980, a 62-year-old man was unluckily struck by lightning,

18
00:00:48,579 --> 00:00:51,159
but luckily it ended up curing his blindness and deafness,

19
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:53,500
being one of the only people in history to have this happen to him.

20
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:54,240
Pretty cool, right?

